WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:06.445
All eyes are on Scarlett Johansson now that&nbsp;
Black Widow has finally hit theaters and Disney+.

00:00:06.445 --> 00:00:11.778
With Black Widow, Natasha Romanoff has&nbsp;
finally got the solo film she always deserved,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.778 --> 00:00:17.847
which takes place between the events of 2016's&nbsp;
Captain America: Civil War and 2018's Avengers:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.847 --> 00:00:22.000
Infinity War. And while everyone knows that&nbsp;
Natasha doesn't make it out of Avengers:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:26.640
Endgame alive, Black Widow is still&nbsp;
a fun ride with a compelling story;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:30.080
one that also introduces a host of&nbsp;
brand new characters to the Marvel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.080 --> 00:00:34.480
Cinematic Universe. The film's post-credits&nbsp;
scene returns the story to the present day,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:39.840
where the audience is painfully reminded&nbsp;
yet again that Natasha is no longer with us.

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:43.520
As difficult as it is for Marvel&nbsp;
fans to relive Natasha's death,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.520 --> 00:00:46.995
it wasn't as hard of a pill for&nbsp;
Johansson to swallow. &nbsp;

00:00:46.995 --> 00:00:51.760
The actress&nbsp;has been busy promoting her new film,&nbsp;
and in an interview with BBC Radio 1,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:56.800
she revealed what it was like to find out that&nbsp;
Natasha was going to meet her demise in Endgame.

00:00:56.800 --> 00:01:00.960
Of course, when the time came to tell Scarlett&nbsp;
Johansson that Black Widow was going to meet&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:05.760
her ultimate fate, there was only one person&nbsp;
who could make the call. Johansson told Radio&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:10.560
1 that Marvel Studios president Kevin Feige&nbsp;
was the one who let her know about Natasha's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:15.334
fate - and she admitted he seemed kind of sad&nbsp;
about being the one to tell her. She said:

00:01:15.334 --> 00:01:20.080
"I think he was nervous to tell me and sad&nbsp;
about it, saying something along the lines of,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:23.920
'We all expected that there would&nbsp;
have to be some big sacrifices.'"

00:01:23.920 --> 00:01:28.468
As far as handling the news, Johansson&nbsp;
apparently took it rather well. She recalled:

00:01:28.468 --> 00:01:32.240
"It didn't surprise me that that was&nbsp;
a choice that Nat would have made.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.240 --> 00:01:36.880
I knew that she had to feel at peace with that&nbsp;
decision and that she was doing it out of love."

00:01:36.880 --> 00:01:39.680
As gutting as it was to lose Natasha in Endgame,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:43.520
fans will have to prepare themselves for&nbsp;
a future without Johansson's character,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.520 --> 00:01:48.880
as the actress has revealed she has absolutely&nbsp;
no plans to return to the role in future. In an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:53.440
interview with Fatherly shortly after the release&nbsp;
of Black Widow, Johansson delivered unsurprising&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.440 --> 00:01:58.868
yet predictable news - that this standalone film&nbsp;
is the last we'll see of this beloved character.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.868 --> 00:02:03.680
She did, however, hint that her relationship&nbsp;
with Marvel is far from over. Johansson said:

00:02:03.680 --> 00:02:07.731
"It feels like a great way to go out&nbsp;
for this chapter of my Marvel identity.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.731 --> 00:02:10.640
I would love to be able to continue&nbsp;
to collaborate with Marvel in other&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.640 --> 00:02:14.000
ways because I think there's just an&nbsp;
incredible wealth of stories there."

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:19.040
Though this may be the end of Johansson's tenure&nbsp;
as Natasha, however, that doesn't mean the moniker&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.040 --> 00:02:23.920
of Black Widow will necessarily be retired&nbsp;
going forward. As fans learned in the film's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.920 --> 00:02:28.320
post-credits scene, Yelena Belova, mourning&nbsp;
the loss of her late adopted sister, has been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.320 --> 00:02:33.440
driven into action by the mysterious Contessa&nbsp;
Valentina Allegra de Fontaine. It's entirely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.440 --> 00:02:39.200
likely that Yelena will step into Natasha's shoes&nbsp;
and take over the mantle in future MCU projects.

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:43.920
Natasha herself, though, leaves behind an&nbsp;
impressive legacy in the MCU - especially&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.920 --> 00:02:48.720
considering her origins. Johansson herself has&nbsp;
even recently criticized how the character was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.720 --> 00:02:52.960
first treated when she arrived in the&nbsp;
MCU. Back in 2010, Johansson joined the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.960 --> 00:02:57.680
superhero franchise in Iron Man 2, but after&nbsp;
fully realizing the character for years,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.680 --> 00:03:01.549
Johansson admitted that she's fairly&nbsp;
unhappy with her character's roots.

00:03:01.549 --> 00:03:03.360
Describing the character's evolution during a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.360 --> 00:03:06.215
roundtable discussion with&nbsp;
the press, Johansson said:

00:03:06.215 --> 00:03:09.200
"I mean, you look back at Iron Man&nbsp;
2 and while it was really fun and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.200 --> 00:03:13.309
had a lot of great moments in it, the&nbsp;
character is so sexualized, you know?"

00:03:13.309 --> 00:03:20.400
"That will be all, Miss Rushman, thank&nbsp;
you very much." "I want one." "No."

00:03:21.040 --> 00:03:22.240
She went on to say:

00:03:22.240 --> 00:03:25.600
"Now people, young girls, are&nbsp;
getting a much more positive message,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.600 --> 00:03:29.600
but it's been incredible to be a part of that&nbsp;
shift and be able to come out the other side&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.600 --> 00:03:34.480
and be a part of that old story, but also&nbsp;
progress. Evolve. I think it's pretty cool."

